(5603813, 808908, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Have to confess my first reaction to this was - ooh, gross.  But that''s only because of the decay and nothing to do with the photograph, so you got a strong reaction which is something.  Interestingly you do not have any 1s.<br/> <br/>It was an interesting interpretation of the challenge topic and perhaps a few voters didn''t think it actually met the challenge.  <br/> <br/>I do think the composition probably hurts this quite a bit.  I think it is framed too tightly and should probably have been taken at a wider angle to give some context.<br/> <br/>The image itself is not really 100% in focus either.  I think for this to work you would need to have shot it so the whole of the skull was in focus.  The way it is now it looks like a mistake not intentional.<br/> <br/>Just some things to consider for the next challenge.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Have to confess my first reaction to this was - ooh, gross.  But that''s only because of the decay and nothing to do with the photograph, so you got a strong reaction which is something.  Interestingly you do not have any 1s. It was an interesting interpretation of the challenge topic and perhaps a few voters didn''t think it actually met the challenge.   I do think the composition probably hurts this quite a bit.  I think it is framed too tightly and should probably have been taken at a wider angle to give some context. The image itself is not really 100% in focus either.  I think for this to work you would need to have shot it so the whole of the skull was in focus.  The way it is now it looks like a mistake not intentional. Just some things to consider for the next challenge. ', '2009-08-08 08:14:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604178, 808905, 26001, '<td valign="top">This is cool on so many levels...composition, colors, exposure, and above all concept.</td>', 'This is cool on so many levels...composition, colors, exposure, and above all concept.', '2009-08-08 15:24:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604774, 809530, 99981, '<td valign="top">Hi, i really loved this shot because of the nice effect on the sky. The 88" exposion add''s so much to this shot, so as the colors of the sky.<br/>I really would like to see more light on the graves, like the CC said down here. Probabbly a pp on them wouldn''t be enough to make them more brighter, right?<br/>Just a question, what about the aperture? Couldn''t it be less then f/16?<br/>Well, i''m not experient, but i think this is a nice shot, and with the graves a little brighter it would probably be on my favorites!<br/>Nice job!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-08-12 12:03:46.</i></td>', 'Hi, i really loved this shot because of the nice effect on the sky. The 88" exposion add''s so much to this shot, so as the colors of the sky.I really would like to see more light on the graves, like the CC said down here. Probabbly a pp on them wouldn''t be enough to make them more brighter, right?Just a question, what about the aperture? Couldn''t it be less then f/16?Well, i''m not experient, but i think this is a nice shot, and with the graves a little brighter it would probably be on my favorites!Nice job!', '2009-08-09 12:49:08.000000', '2009-08-12 13:03:46.000000', 0),
(5607754, 809930, 49244, '<td valign="top">Wow I am actually really stoked on my placement for a number of reasons. I took this photo while I was out on the boat and didn''t know what the challenge was going to be, I just happen to have a photo that worked. I know I should of used a larger depth of field, which I did on my other salmon shots, but this one worked out better compositionally. Another problem I have is editing with my basic macbook, the LCD interupts my color and contrast so badly I never know what it is really going to look like, I need to purchase a external monitor. Editing was really basic, small crop and few minor adjustments to contrast and brightness. I am out at sea again and I left my laptop back in town otherwise I would tell you specifically, but I wont be back until the begining of september sorry.</td>', 'Wow I am actually really stoked on my placement for a number of reasons. I took this photo while I was out on the boat and didn''t know what the challenge was going to be, I just happen to have a photo that worked. I know I should of used a larger depth of field, which I did on my other salmon shots, but this one worked out better compositionally. Another problem I have is editing with my basic macbook, the LCD interupts my color and contrast so badly I never know what it is really going to look like, I need to purchase a external monitor. Editing was really basic, small crop and few minor adjustments to contrast and brightness. I am out at sea again and I left my laptop back in town otherwise I would tell you specifically, but I wont be back until the begining of september sorry.', '2009-08-11 18:57:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5609652, 809530, 28359, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a good finish and a excellent shot!</td>', 'Congrats on a good finish and a excellent shot!', '2009-08-12 22:11:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5611530, 809521, 96509, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments. The lower right white thing is an angel statue, the idea was to have sligthly out of focus, not as much as in this shot, but just after i took this one I was kick off of the cemetery so I couldn''t retake it.</td>', 'thanks for the comments. The lower right white thing is an angel statue, the idea was to have sligthly out of focus, not as much as in this shot, but just after i took this one I was kick off of the cemetery so I couldn''t retake it.', '2009-08-14 10:05:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5611982, 809780, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from the C Club<br/> <br/>Powerful POV here.  The grain is very dominant in this, I think just a tiny bit less would have given a little impact.  Also your cropping could be more dramatic in this shot.  Crop out the shower curtain and the soap dish, and BAM you are full force on with your ''body''<br/> <br/>I do not think there is anything else in post processing that you can do, as this seems perfect for this shot</td>', 'HI from the C Club Powerful POV here.  The grain is very dominant in this, I think just a tiny bit less would have given a little impact.  Also your cropping could be more dramatic in this shot.  Crop out the shower curtain and the soap dish, and BAM you are full force on with your ''body'' I do not think there is anything else in post processing that you can do, as this seems perfect for this shot', '2009-08-14 20:31:47.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5612390, 810001, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the C Club!<br/> <br/>What an interesting shot, i love all the greens with that vivid white.<br/> <br/>You shallow DOF works really well here with this subject.  But I couldn''t actually tell what it was until I read your notes. . More focus on the actual insects would have helped , when i looked for a while, i could tell it was a wasp type thing and spider, but the back of the body of the wasp was out of focus.  If it had been in focus then it would have slapped me in the face and screamed spider eating wasp. <br/> <br/>Your post processing is good, just needs a little more sharpness, the colours are outstanding. So a little more DOF would have brought this score right up there. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the C Club! What an interesting shot, i love all the greens with that vivid white. You shallow DOF works really well here with this subject.  But I couldn''t actually tell what it was until I read your notes. . More focus on the actual insects would have helped , when i looked for a while, i could tell it was a wasp type thing and spider, but the back of the body of the wasp was out of focus.  If it had been in focus then it would have slapped me in the face and screamed spider eating wasp.  Your post processing is good, just needs a little more sharpness, the colours are outstanding. So a little more DOF would have brought this score right up there.  ', '2009-08-15 11:41:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5617910, 808752, 108811, '<td valign="top">thanks JulietNN and others for Ur comments,<br/> <br/>to make it clear it is a ''dead pig'' as i ve mentioned in the description, as lot of people are  confused about.<br/> <br/>i clicked it as it was...and i din added any thing to it...<br/> <br/>and julien i didn''t crop it cos the whole thing gives it a ''death bed'' kinda feel...and that''s what i wanted to capture.<br/> <br/>this is from my sereis called death.<br/> <br/>i appreciate ur views and crtique.<br/> <br/>thanks <br/> <br/>paule''<br/> <br/>and surely i ll put more.</td>', 'thanks JulietNN and others for Ur comments, to make it clear it is a ''dead pig'' as i ve mentioned in the description, as lot of people are  confused about. i clicked it as it was...and i din added any thing to it... and julien i didn''t crop it cos the whole thing gives it a ''death bed'' kinda feel...and that''s what i wanted to capture. this is from my sereis called death. i appreciate ur views and crtique. thanks  paule'' and surely i ll put more.', '2009-08-20 03:31:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5622364, 809747, 34659, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool photo...  Beautifully presented and love the DOF.<br/> <br/>Really a chilling image.  :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-08-24 20:29:30.</i></td>', 'This is a very cool photo...  Beautifully presented and love the DOF. Really a chilling image.  :-)', '2009-08-24 21:28:53.000000', '2009-08-24 21:29:30.000000', 0),
(5634688, 810183, 106233, '<td valign="top">no.</td>', 'no.', '2009-09-03 16:03:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5653455, 809720, 62357, '<td valign="top">Hello Nicole<br/> <br/>Greetings from the critique club.<br/> <br/>I got the chance to critique this from the club archives, which is why it is coming so long after the challenge.<br/> <br/>I think this was a good first entry in what I think was quite a difficult challenge.  It''s never easy to portray death photographically (at least that is my opinion).  <br/> <br/>As far as the image goes, I think your idea was a good one.  I do believe you could have increased your score a little bit with some changes to your camera set up and some some small tweaks in post processing.<br/> <br/>Looking at the settings on your camera, I think you were probably hand holding the camera for this image, right?  If you had used a tripod (even if you don''t have one, something solid to place the camera on could work almost as well) I think you could have increased your f number to something like f8 which would have increased the depth of field a bit.  I know you would have needed to reduce the shutter speed, but if you were using a tripod this would be OK.  I think ultimately it would have resulted in a sharper image, which is a big help on DPC.  (Voters like things sharp typically).  <br/> <br/>A quick adjustment using a levels adjustment layer (assuming some sort of photoshop or other software is available to you) would have rendered the whites a bit whiter.  As it stands, the whites have a greyish feel to them and this makes the image feel a bit flat and lacking contrast.  <br/> <br/>Overall I think this was a good first entry.  Keep it up.<br/> <br/>Feel free to pm me if you want further comment or clarification on anything.</td>', 'Hello Nicole Greetings from the critique club. I got the chance to critique this from the club archives, which is why it is coming so long after the challenge. I think this was a good first entry in what I think was quite a difficult challenge.  It''s never easy to portray death photographically (at least that is my opinion).   As far as the image goes, I think your idea was a good one.  I do believe you could have increased your score a little bit with some changes to your camera set up and some some small tweaks in post processing. Looking at the settings on your camera, I think you were probably hand holding the camera for this image, right?  If you had used a tripod (even if you don''t have one, something solid to place the camera on could work almost as well) I think you could have increased your f number to something like f8 which would have increased the depth of field a bit.  I know you would have needed to reduce the shutter speed, but if you were using a tripod this would be OK.  I think ultimately it would have resulted in a sharper image, which is a big help on DPC.  (Voters like things sharp typically).   A quick adjustment using a levels adjustment layer (assuming some sort of photoshop or other software is available to you) would have rendered the whites a bit whiter.  As it stands, the whites have a greyish feel to them and this makes the image feel a bit flat and lacking contrast.   Overall I think this was a good first entry.  Keep it up. Feel free to pm me if you want further comment or clarification on anything.', '2009-09-19 04:48:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5714352, 810186, 88523, '<td valign="top">Really cool...</td>', 'Really cool...', '2009-11-04 17:14:09.000000', NULL, 0);
